    "content": "The 45th Annual Dallas St. Patrick's Parade & Festival is on Saturday, March 14, 2026, along Greenville Avenue. The parade starts at 11 AM at Blackwell Street and ends at SMU Blvd around 2 PM, featuring over 90 floats and live music, while the surrounding festival runs 9 AM–3 PM. Parade and Event Details: Route: The parade proceeds down Greenville Avenue from Park Lane to SMU Boulevard. Festival & Floats: The parade features over 90 floats, food trucks, and family-friendly activities. Key Events: In addition to the main parade, the event features the St. Patrick's Day Dash 5K, as noted in a D Magazine article and on WFAA. D Magazine article WFAA Block Party: The Lower Greenville St. Patrick's Day Block Party occurs near the parade route. Lower Greenville St. Patrick's Day Block Party Important Tips & Logistics: 交通 (Transportation): Major road closures include Greenville Avenue from Park Lane to Mockingbird Lane. DART: Attendees are encouraged to use DART, specifically the Park Lane or Lovers Lane stations, say CBS News and dallasstpp.com. CBS News dallasstpp.com Parking: Street parking is limited, so parking at DART stations or pre-paid lots is recommended. Block Party Info: The Lower Greenville Block Party is for ages 21+ and requires a cash entry fee. Lower Greenville Block Party For the latest updates and schedules, check the Official Dallas St. Patrick's Parade Facebook page or the Visit Dallas event page. Official Dallas St. Patrick's Parade Facebook page Visit Dallas event page",
